#!/bin/bash
java -jar bx-agent/target/bx-agent-1.0.0-SNAPSHOT.jar \
  -s examples/pn2pnw/PetriNet.ecore \
  -t examples/pn2pnw/PetriNetWeighted.ecore \
  -o generated \
  -e incrementalID \
  -d "Transform a PetriNet (pn) to a WeightedPetriNet (pnw). Both models share the same root structure: a Net containing NetElements (Transitions and Places) via the 'elements' containment reference. The root Net and its Transition and Place elements map 1:1 with their attributes (name, noOfTokens). In pn, connections between Transitions and Places are represented as direct references: Transition.trgT2P (Transition→Place, eOpposite Place.srcT2P) and Place.trgP2T (Place→Transition, eOpposite Transition.srcP2T). In pnw, these connections are materialized as explicit edge objects: TPEdge (with fromTransition and toPlace) and PTEdge (with fromPlace and toTransition), both of which are NetElements contained in Net.elements. TPEdge and PTEdge have a weight attribute (EInt, default 1) inherited from the abstract Edge class. Use edgeMaterializationMappings: map Transition.trgT2P to TPEdge (edgeFromRef=fromTransition, edgeToRef=toPlace, edgeContainerRef=elements) and Place.trgP2T to PTEdge (edgeFromRef=fromPlace, edgeToRef=toTransition, edgeContainerRef=elements). Do NOT include TPEdge or PTEdge in typeMappings or referenceMappings. Do NOT include trgT2P, srcT2P, trgP2T, srcP2T, outTPEdges, inTPEdges, outPTEdges, or inPTEdges in referenceMappings — all connectivity is handled exclusively via edgeMaterializationMappings. The abstract types NetElement and NamedElement are supertypes and must not appear in typeMappings."
